---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Mike Gilmore"
  description="About Mike Gilmore: technical delivery, systems analysis, customer solutions, cloud infrastructure, and SaaS reliability."
>
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>I like the work between the requirement and the reality.</h1>
    <p>
      My career has crossed customer operations, enterprise implementation, cloud delivery, and site reliability. The part I keep gravitating toward is the same:
      understand what people are trying to accomplish, find the technical and process constraints, and make the path forward clearer.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="shell page-grid">
    <article class="detail-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I think</p>
      <h2>Start with the problem, then decide how technical the answer needs to be.</h2>
      <p>
        Sometimes the answer is an API flow, SQL validation, cloud configuration, or production signal. Sometimes it is a better requirement,
        clearer ownership, a readiness check, or a process that stops the same issue from coming back. I am comfortable moving between those layers.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="detail-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I work with teams</p>
      <h2>Translate across boundaries without turning everything into a handoff.</h2>
      <p>
        I work best where customers, implementation teams, Product, Engineering, and operations need enough shared context to make a good decision.
        Clear discovery, documentation, prioritization, and follow-through matter as much as the technical diagnosis.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="detail-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">What I bring</p>
      <h2>Customer perspective backed by engineering context.</h2>
      <p>
        The engineering background gives me enough depth to investigate integrations, authentication, SQL, cloud infrastructure, observability,
        and production behavior. The customer and operations background keeps the focus on whether the solution is understandable, supportable, and useful.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/work/">Explore selected work</a>
        <a class="button button--secondary" href="/resume/">View experience</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
